 "answer_key": "Read off each product's own openFDA records, as in seed/holdout_profiles: the approval year from the earliest ORIG submission with AP status in drugsFDA, the route from the label endpoint's openfda block, the therapy area from the first indication the label lists. The application number on each row is what to fetch to check it.",
 "independence": "Route, approval year, era and the peer count are facts of the cited records. moa_class and indication_area are groupings a reader assigned from the same labels the pipeline reads - an independent reading of a shared source, not an independent source - and are scored on which products they group, never on wording.",
 "peer_counts_are_within_this_set": "marketed_peers_at_launch counts the products in this file approved earlier in the same indication_area, so it holds only for a run whose catalogue is this set. Three products share one area across three approval years, so a derivation that always answers zero fails here.",
